Here is a basic implementation of the web component you requested using Shadow DOM:

HTML:

```html
<x-details>
  <span slot="header">Header here</span>
  <div slot="intro">intro part always visible</div>
  <div slot="details">details part - visible when expanded</div>
</x-details>
```

JavaScript:

```javascript
class XDetails extends HTMLElement {
  constructor() {
    super();
    this.attachShadow({ mode: 'open' });
    this.isOpen = false;

    this.shadowRoot.innerHTML = `
      <style>
        :host {
          display: block;
        }
        .header {
          font-size: 1.2em;
          border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc;
          cursor: pointer;
        }
        .header:before {
          content: ' ';
          display: inline-block;
          width: 16px;
          height: 16px;
          margin-right: 8px;
          background: #ccc;
          border: 1px solid #aaa;
          box-sizing: border-box;
          vertical-align: middle;
        }
        .header[open]:before {
          content: ' ';
          background: #fff;
          border: 1px solid #aaa;
          box-sizing: border-box;
        }
        .intro {
          margin-bottom: 8px;
        }
        .details {
          display: none;
        }
        .details[open] {
          display: block;
        }
        .expand-more {
          display: none;
        }
        .expand-more[open] {
          display: block;
        }
      </style>
      <div class="header" part="header">
        <slot name="header"></slot>
      </div>
      <div class="intro" part="intro">
        <slot name="intro"></slot>
      </div>
      <div class="details" part="details">
        <slot name="details"></slot>
      </div>
      <button class="expand-more" part="expand-more">Expand More</button>
    `;

    this.header = this.shadowRoot.querySelector('.header');
    this.intro = this.shadowRoot.querySelector('.intro');
    this.details = this.shadowRoot.querySelector('.details');
    this.expandMore = this.shadowRoot.querySelector('.expand-more');

    this.header.addEventListener('click', () => this.toggle());
    this.expandMore.addEventListener('click', () => this.toggle());
  }

  toggle() {
    this.isOpen = !this.isOpen;
    this.header.setAttribute('open', this.isOpen);
    this.details.setAttribute('open', this.isOpen);
    this.expandMore.setAttribute('open', this.isOpen);
  }
}

customElements.define('x-details', XDetails);
```

This code defines a custom element `x-details` that uses Shadow DOM to encapsulate its structure and styles. The component has three slots for the header, intro, and details content, and it uses CSS to style these elements. The component also has a toggle function that is called when the header or expand more button is clicked, which toggles the `open` attribute on the header, details, and expand more elements, which in turn controls their display. The `open` attribute is also used to style the header and expand more elements differently when the component is open.

