### Evaluation

Assistant B is better. Its implementation covers the requested slots, keeps the intro visible, hides the details while collapsed, provides a square plus/minus indicator, styles the header, and supplies the requested “expand more” button. It also updates the button label when expanded.

However, B has a functional bug: it attaches click handlers to both `.indicator` and its parent `.header`. Clicking the indicator fires both handlers because the event bubbles, so the component toggles twice and ends up in its original state. The indicator-specific listener should be removed; the header listener already handles clicks on it. B could also improve accessibility by using a semantic button for the header and setting `aria-expanded`.

Assistant A has more serious issues. Its pseudo-element never displays a `+` or `−`, and it uses `setAttribute('open', false)`, which still creates the attribute. As a result, the `[open]` selectors match even when the value is `"false"`. Also, the “expand more” button is hidden initially and shown only when open—the opposite of the requested collapsed state. These flaws make A’s implementation fail key requirements.

[[B>>A]]

